# React Native component rules

## Always
- Every text string is inside `<Text>` — never render a bare string in a `<View>`
- `{count > 0 && <X/>}` never `{count && <X/>}` (renders `0` → crash)
- Be explicit with `flex-row` — `flexDirection` defaults to `column`
- Wrap truncating text in `<View className="flex-1">` (`flexShrink` defaults to 0)
- Interactive elements get `accessibilityRole` and `accessibilityLabel`
- Touch targets ≥44pt — use `hitSlop` on small icon buttons
- Handle safe areas with `useSafeAreaInsets()`
- `keyboardShouldPersistTaps="handled"` on any ScrollView containing a form

## Use / don't use
| Use | Not |
|---|---|
| `Pressable` | `TouchableOpacity` |
| `expo-image` | `Image` from react-native |
| `FlashList` | `.map()` for data lists |
| `active:` | `hover:` |
| `gap-*` | `space-x-*` |
| Reanimated worklets | JS-state-driven animation |

## Lists
- Memoize rows with `React.memo`
- `useCallback` for `renderItem` and row callbacks — no inline arrows
- `getItemType` when rows are heterogeneous
- `recyclingKey` on images inside rows

## Styling
- Semantic tokens only — no hardcoded colors
- Container styles and text styles are separate (no cascade in React Native)
- Prefer borders over shadows for cross-platform consistency

## Screens
- Screens in `app/` are thin — compose hooks and components
- Business logic goes in `src/features/*/utils.ts` so it's unit-testable
